{
  "description": "OmniClaude Core Hooks - OMN-13244 measurement baseline with the OMN-13856, OMN-14330, OMN-15062, OMN-15213, OMN-16277, OMN-16162, OMN-16471, OMN-16478, OMN-17006, OMN-17168, OMN-17190, OMN-19607, OMN-17207, and OMN-17020 carve-outs, plus the carve-outs numbered by ticket (OMN-17499, OMN-17942, OMN-17957, OMN-18335 and the OMN-13856 item 4 actor-line guard). Every context-injection/measurement hook the OMN-13244 baseline unregistered stays DISABLED unless a carve-out re-registers it, and every other script stays on disk, so re-registration remains a pure config change. AUTHORITY NOTE (OMN-17020): plugins/onex/hooks/contracts/hook_inventory.yaml is the typed inventory of what is registered here and what is dark -- every registration in this file must be declared there with an owner, a ticket, a purpose and either an end-to-end canary or a stated reason one cannot be run, and every deliberate disable must carry the four STANDING RULE fields as typed data (owner, reason, an absolute review_by date, and a restoration naming its kind, its re-enable ticket and its action). The hook-inventory gate fails closed on any drift between the two, so a registration added here without a declaration there, or a hook quietly removed from here, is a failing check rather than something a reader has to notice. The reasoning behind each carve-out lives in its inventory entry, in the registered script's own header and in its ticket, not in this string. STANDING RULE (OMN-17006): any future baseline-style disable of a hook registered here MUST land in the same change as an expiry condition and a named re-enable ticket, and that record MUST name all four of: OWNER -- the role or lane accountable for restoring it; REASON -- why this specific hook is off, not merely that it is; EXPIRY -- the absolute condition or date after which the disable is void; RESTORATION -- the automatic behaviour that re-registers the hook once the expiry is reached, and the re-enable ticket that tracks it. A disable with no expiry and no re-enable ticket is how OMN-13244 left enforcement dark for months while the rule it enforced was corrected by hand about 61 times. The two carve-outs that are stopgaps by construction keep their records here as well as in the inventory. The SessionStart goal-surface hook (OMN-17168, session_start_goal_surface.sh; print-only, exits 0 on every user-visible outcome, so it can neither refuse nor delay a session), per the STANDING RULE above, its own carve-out record: OWNER -- the operator / the session-goal lane; REASON -- the durable session goal is invisible at session start, so it is remembered rather than read, which is the same dark-enforcement class as OMN-13244 itself; EXPIRY -- when OMN-17169 lands the goal projection and the goal file stops being the source of truth; RESTORATION -- at that expiry the hook is REPOINTED from the file read to the projection read and stays registered under this same entry, and OMN-17169 carries that repoint as a closeout AC. The local-capture pair (post_tool_use_auto_checkpoint.sh and post_tool_use_changeset_guard.sh, registered LAST in PostToolUse on the Bash matcher, after the OMN-16277 secret-redaction guard; they write only to the local filesystem, emit nothing on stdout and publish nothing to the bus), per the STANDING RULE above, the OMN-17207 carve-out record: OWNER -- the observability ladder lane (epic OMN-16176); REASON -- a tool call is recorded without the tree change it made, so every claim of work is unfalsifiable from that record, and these two hooks restore the git-delta and changeset-magnitude fields locally while the bus half is designed; EXPIRY -- when OMN-17207 lands work.delta events on the bus and OMN-17209 clears the egress and redaction gate that keeps these payloads local today; RESTORATION -- at that expiry these two hooks are SUPERSEDED, not merely unregistered: the local checkpoint files and the changeset series are replaced by work.delta events and their projection, and OMN-17207 carries that removal as a closeout AC.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "^mcp__linear-server__(save_issue|update_issue)$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_done_flip_guard.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_ticket_creation_gate.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_bash_guards.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "^(Workflow|Agent)$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_agent_model_guard.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "^(Task|Agent|Workflow)$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_lane_open.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "^SendMessage$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_lane_liveness_guard.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "^(Bash|Edit|Write|NotebookEdit|MultiEdit)$",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_overseer_foreground_block.sh",
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Skill",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/scripts/pre_tool_use_skill_started.sh"
